[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: 3.e3"]
[ECO "D30"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "c5-break,isolated-pawn,qgd-setup"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3.e3"]
[Start "orthodox 2...e6"]

3. e3 { A solid move that guards c4 and d4, but it shuts in the c1 bishop behind the pawn. } 3... Nf6 { Develops and watches e4. Black plays the same set-up as against 3.Nc3. } 4. Nf3 ( 4. Nc3 { The same position as 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.e3, so Black plays the same moves: ...Be7, ...O-O, then ...dxc4 and ...c5 once the bishop is on d3. } 4... Be7 5. Nf3 O-O ) 4... Be7 5. Bd3 ( 5. Nc3 O-O ) ( 5. Nbd2 O-O 6. Bd3 c5 { The knight on d2 does not guard d4, so Black hits it. } ) ( 5. Be2 O-O 6. O-O dxc4 7. Bxc4 c5 ) 5... O-O 6. O-O dxc4 { Takes on c4 now that the bishop has moved to d3, so it has to move again. } 7. Bxc4 c5 { Strikes at d4, the usual freeing break in this set-up. } 8. Qe2 ( 8. Nc3 { The same position as 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.e3 Be7 5.Nf3 O-O 6.Bd3 dxc4 7.Bxc4 c5 8.O-O. } 8... cxd4 9. exd4 Nc6 ) ( 8. dxc5 Bxc5 { Takes back, and the bishop is active on c5. The position is level with no weaknesses on either side. } ) ( 8. b3 cxd4 9. Nxd4 a6 ) 8... cxd4 9. exd4 Nc6 { White has an isolated pawn on d4: no pawn on the c- or e-file can defend it. Plan: ...b6 and ...Bb7, a knight to d5 or b4-d5, and trade pieces, because the fewer pieces there are, the weaker the d4 pawn. } *
